  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Differentiating the given equation of the curve\n\\(\\begin{aligned}\n& 4 x-6 y \\cdot(\\mathrm{dy} / \\mathrm{dx})=0 \\quad \\therefore \\mathrm{dy} / \\mathrm{dx}=2 \\mathrm{x} / 3 \\mathrm{y} \\\\\n& \\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{dy}}{\\mathrm{dx}}\\right)_{(3,2)}=\\frac{2}{3} \\cdot \\frac{3}{2}=1\n\\end{aligned}\\)",
